WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:06.529
According to the Oxfam report, the number
of billionaires has doubled in the ten years

00:00:06.529 --> 00:00:08.990
since the financial crisis hit.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:14.169
It also highlights that the 26 wealthiest
people on the planet now own as much as the

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:20.530
3.8 billion people who make up the poorer
half of humanity.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:26.730
This is unacceptable and there are solutions
and the solutions lie in the hands of government

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:33.730
to tax wealth, to stop tax dodging, to plough
the money into these public services and give

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:38.960
everyone a fair chance to be part of the global
economy.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.320
Oxfam publishes its inequality report every
year shortly before the start of the World

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.620
Economic Forum in Davos.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.960
It's an attempt to highlight the issue with
the politicians and business heavyweights

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.190
meeting up in the Swiss resort.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:58.120
But some economists have criticized the study
for implying there are simple solutions to

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.219
a complex problem.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:05.100
Other factors also play a major role in wealth
inequality, they say...for example in the

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.390
African nations that are home to some of the
world's poorest.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:14.469
There, unstable political systems, a corrupt
elite, civil war and poor education structures

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:16.780
continue to have an ongoing impact

